# Zones which are built and published but which the renderers should not load.
#
#   <zone> <reason>   # note
#
# Everything built is published either way. A zone listed here stays
# downloadable and stops being drawn: the tile servers take a zone that leaves
# the manifest out of their rasters and out of their contour database.
#
# The reason is required, and one of:
#
#   withdrawn   the territory has been withdrawn or wiped, so the contours
#               describe ground that is no longer there
#   quality     the input squares are not good enough to render from
#   wip         work in progress - being drawn, reviewed or recovered, and not
#               ready to appear on the map yet
#
# Date the note. A zone with no reason recorded stays inactive long after
# anyone remembers what the reason was, which is how zone-tekan came to have
# five years of published data that was never drawn.
#
# Leaving a zone out of the render is not the same as retiring it. To stop
# building a zone at all, move its squares out of osm-squares; its published
# output then stays as it was and nothing regenerates it.
